---
import LegalPage from '../components/LegalPage.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---

<LegalPage accent="License" title="Code license" description={`The license for the code versions of ${site.name} templates: one project, no resale, no sharing.`} updated="November 3, 2026">
  <p>
    This is the license for the code versions of {site.name} templates (each one a "Template"), sold through
    Contra. The seller (the "Licensor") is Vladimir Kotenev, trading as {site.name}. The license does not apply to the
    Framer versions, which follow the license on their Framer page. The same text is in the file LICENSE.md inside every
    download.
  </p>

  <h2>What you get</h2>
  <p>
    A non-exclusive, worldwide, perpetual license to use the Template to build <strong>one</strong> website or app
    landing page (a "Project"), for yourself or for one client. The license starts when you have paid in full.
  </p>

  <h2>You can</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Edit the code, text, colors and images however you like.</li>
    <li>Use the finished Project for commercial purposes, including selling products or services on it.</li>
    <li>Hand the finished Project to your one client. The client owns the Project, not the Template files as a template.</li>
    <li>Keep backups of the files for your own Project.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>You cannot</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Resell, sublicense, rent, lend, give away or share the Template or any part of it, changed or not, free or paid.</li>
    <li>Use the Template for a second Project. Each extra Project needs its own license.</li>
    <li>Put the files in a public repository or a file-sharing site. A repository that holds only your finished Project is fine.</li>
    <li>Turn the Template, or a version of it, into a template, theme, starter, boilerplate, kit, UI library or website builder, or into any product that lets others reuse the files as a base.</li>
    <li>Present the Template as your own design to sell as a template.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Ownership</h2>
  <p>
    The Template stays the property of the Licensor. This license gives you the right to use it as described above and
    nothing more.
  </p>

  <h2>Third-party parts</h2>
  <p>
    The Template uses the Inter font (SIL Open Font License 1.1) and Lucide icons (ISC License). They keep their own
    licenses. The README of each Template lists its credits.
  </p>

  <h2>Images</h2>
  <p>
    Demo images, screenshots and photos in the files show the layout. Replace them with your own before you publish,
    unless the README says an image is free to use.
  </p>

  <h2>Updates</h2>
  <p>
    We may publish new versions. If we do, you can get them from your purchase page on Contra. Updates are a courtesy,
    not a promise.
  </p>

  <h2>Payment and refunds</h2>
  <p>The Templates are digital products and all sales are final. See the <a href="/refunds/">refund policy</a>.</p>

  <h2>No warranty</h2>
  <p>
    The Template is provided as is, without warranty of any kind. To the extent the law allows, the Licensor is not
    liable for any damage that comes from using it.
  </p>

  <h2>Ending the license</h2>
  <p>If you break these terms, the license ends and you must stop using the Template and delete the files.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions about the license: <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.</p>
</LegalPage>
